4. Use the delta function property to simplify $\mathbf{I} = \frac{2\mu_0}{3} \mu_p |\Psi(0)|^2$. 
5. Substitute $\mu_p = 1.41 \times 10^{-26} \, \text{J/T}$, $a_0 = 5.29 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{m}$, and $\mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{H/m}$ into $|\mathbf{I}| = \frac{2\mu_0 \mu_p}{3\pi a_0^3}$ for the final value.
</think>
