4. Convert t = 10 minutes to seconds (600 s).  
5. Calculate the exponent λ_total × t.  
6. Compute N(t) = 5×10³⁴ × exp(-λ_total × t).  
7. Multiply λ_α by N(t) to obtain the alpha decay activity in Bq (decays per second).  
This ensures unit consistency, isolates alpha activity, and accounts for exponential depletion of N(t).
</think>
